WHAT THE REPORTER ACTUALLY SAW (the part still worth an issue)
The finding was real, but not about the source file. It was observed against the
MARKETPLACE CACHE at plugin 0.16.5 -- the clone under
`~/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/kipi/`, which is what Claude Code actually loads.
The skeleton was fixed and the clone was never refreshed, so a fresh session kept
being told to refuse working commands. That is skeleton -> clone version drift,
and nothing in the repo detects it.

Editing SKILL.md cannot fix that: the file is already right. The clone needs a
refresh (a runtime `/plugin marketplace update`), and the durable fix is a drift
check that compares the installed clone's plugin.json version against the
skeleton's and fails when they diverge. Neither is in this issue's allowed files.

I could not verify the clone's current state from here -- this session's sandbox
refuses reads outside the worktree (`Read ~/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/kipi/
